---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import Pill from '../ui/Pill.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s21b-layer-pods-commands"
  chapter="Layers"
  title="Pods — Commands"
  notes="Pod state deep dive: get wide, describe for events, jsonpath for phase and conditions. Myth: Running means healthy — can be Running with failing probes or CrashLoopBackOff."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-6">
    <section>
      <h3 class="mb-3 font-display text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-deck-cyan">Typical commands</h3>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="bash"
        caption="Pod state deep dive"
        code={`kubectl get pod <pod> -n <ns> -o wide
kubectl describe pod <pod> -n <ns>
kubectl get pod <pod> -n <ns> -o jsonpath='{.status.phase}{"\\n"}{range .status.conditions[*]}{.type}={.status}{"\\n"}{end}'`}
      />
    </section>

    <Callout type="myth">
      Running means healthy. A pod can be Running with failing probes, partial init success, or containers in CrashLoopBackOff.
    </Callout>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-deck-border/60 pt-4">
      <Pill tone="amber">Decision hint</Pill>
      <span class="text-lg text-deck-muted">Trust conditions over the STATUS column — Ready=False is your early warning.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</Slide>
